WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.080
Can you call Dwayne Johnson "little brother" and&nbsp;
survive? Vin Diesel thinks he can. This is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.440
complete timeline of the explosive feud between&nbsp;
Hollywood's biggest and baldest action stars.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.280
The year is 2011. A new show called&nbsp;
"Game of Thrones" is airing on HBO.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.920
Adele's "Rolling in the Deep" is on top of&nbsp;
the charts. And a street racing franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.640
called "Fast and Furious" is coming off&nbsp;
its most recent successful installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.280
the 2009 film "Fast &amp; Furious." But that's&nbsp;
nothing compared to the fifth film that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.800
about to premiere — aptly titled "Fast Five" -–&nbsp;
which helps propel the series to become one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.640
most successful franchises in history. There are&nbsp;
many reasons for the film's stunning success, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.280
one obvious reason is the addition of former WWE&nbsp;
superstar Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson to the cast.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.680
"Fast Five" kicks off a golden age for the&nbsp;
franchise, feeding into the successes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:59.360
"Fast &amp; Furious 6" and "Furious 7." All three&nbsp;
films feature The Rock's Luke Hobbs character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.520
and his onscreen dynamic with Diesel, Paul Walker,&nbsp;
and the rest of the cast is compelling. Tragedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.280
struck the series in the form of Walker's death&nbsp;
in 2013, but his friends and co-stars rallied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.400
behind his legacy and pushed forward. The future&nbsp;
of the franchise still looked a bit uncertain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.280
but an eighth core film, "The Fate of the&nbsp;
Furious," was announced and entered production.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.520
On August 8, 2016, one week before production&nbsp;
wrapped for "The Fate of the Furious,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.760
Johnson took to Instagram and made a&nbsp;
post that he then quickly deleted. In it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.120
he praised many members of the film's cast&nbsp;
and crew while also calling out a few unnamed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.160
people with particularly colorful language.&nbsp;
After praising all the women he starred with,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.760
Johnson turned his attention to&nbsp;
his male co-stars, saying that

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.000
"Some conduct themselves as stand up men&nbsp;
and true professionals, while others don't.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.880
The ones that don't are too chicken s**t to&nbsp;
do anything about it anyway. Candy asses."

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:55.920
He added that

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.200
"When you watch this movie next April&nbsp;
and it seems like I'm not acting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.880
some of these scenes and my blood&nbsp;
is legit boiling — you're right."

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.040
A TMZ report published shortly after the&nbsp;
post was made claimed that the man Johnson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.360
was targeting with his pro wrestling style&nbsp;
insult was none other than Diesel himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.640
and that the two actors had major tension on set&nbsp;
throughout the production process. On August 10,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.000
Johnson made another Instagram post that seemingly&nbsp;
swept his previous frustrations under the rug.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.440
In it, he thanked the whole cast and&nbsp;
crew for their hard work and said that

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.800
"...like with any team — that's a&nbsp;
family — there's gonna be conflict.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.280
Family is gonna have differences of opinion&nbsp;
and fundamental core beliefs ... I was raised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.200
on healthy conflict and welcome it. And&nbsp;
like any family, we get better from it."

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.640
Things, at least for the moment,&nbsp;
seemed to have calmed back down.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.560
"We're family. We got a problem,&nbsp;
we deal with it together."

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.960
Despite Johnson's apparent attempt to&nbsp;
squash the beef, the story he'd made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.240
public refused to die down. Diesel shared&nbsp;
a vague response to Instagram on August 10,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.440
promising the public that he would,&nbsp;
quote, "tell you everything soon."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.600
Costar Michelle Rodriguez then confirmed in an&nbsp;
interview with People that there had been tension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.360
between the two, but that she believed they&nbsp;
cared about each other and would work it out.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.720
"You never turn your back on family, and I wanna&nbsp;
thank you for never turning your back on me."

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.520
On August 19, Johnson made another Instagram post&nbsp;
after filming had officially wrapped, in which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:23.120
thanked many of his costars in the film by name,&nbsp;
notably excluding Diesel. Though the insult was by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.480
omission, it seemed clear that whatever had gone&nbsp;
on between the two actors was still unresolved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.560
even if they'd put their differences aside for&nbsp;
the sake of the film. Speculation continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:36.800
to circulate, but there wasn't any new fuel&nbsp;
to pour on the fire for a couple of months.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.880
In a November 19, 2016 interview with the Los&nbsp;
Angeles Times, Johnson discussed his initial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.440
post and his dynamic with Diesel. When asked&nbsp;
about the comments he'd made, Johnson responded,

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.640
"I've been in the game a long time. Would&nbsp;
Universal [Pictures] have preferred that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.400
didn't happen? Sure, we talked about it.&nbsp;
The irony is after that and as they do their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.960
tracking and all their analysis, the interest&nbsp;
shot through the roof to a whole other level."

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.000
Johnson's implication seemed&nbsp;
to be that, whether or not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.080
it was the original motivation for the&nbsp;
post, the publicity generated by his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.080
online feuding only did good things for&nbsp;
"The Fate of the Furious." To be fair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:15.920
The Rock is a showman, and he came up through a&nbsp;
WWE organization where beefing was, and still is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.560
a huge part of publicity. The actual tension&nbsp;
between the two stars likely still existed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.640
but it seemed as though Johnson was no&nbsp;
longer interested in fanning the flames.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:31.200
"I know you guys are a family. I'm offering&nbsp;
you the chance to make that family whole again."

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:38.240
On April 7, 2017 -– just days before "The Fate&nbsp;
of the Furious" was released globally -– Diesel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.200
resurrected the previous year's feud in an&nbsp;
interview with USA Today. His words sounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:48.720
kind-hearted at first glance, but they had a&nbsp;
decidedly backhanded quality to them. He said,

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.320
"I don't think the world really realizes&nbsp;
how close we are, in a weird way. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.640
know he appreciates how much I work this&nbsp;
franchise. In my house, he's Uncle Dwayne."

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.000
That's all pretty innocuous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.480
but Diesel quickly made it clear who he saw&nbsp;
as the true alpha in their relationship.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.520
"I protect the franchise. I&nbsp;
protect everybody including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.400
Dwayne. I protected Dwayne&nbsp;
more than he'll ever know."

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.960
And then, he played the little brother card.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.040
"Dwayne has only got one Vin in his life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.200
Dwayne Johnson only has one big brother&nbsp;
in this film world and that's me."

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.480
While it's true that Diesel is&nbsp;
a few years older than Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.720
referring to The Rock as a little&nbsp;
brother is, in a word, harsh.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.840
"Oh, my, my bad. I'm sorry,&nbsp;
I'm just processing. Brother?"

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.560
Though Diesel claimed camaraderie&nbsp;
with Johnson throughout the interview,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.680
it seemed clear what message he was sending –-&nbsp;
there's only one king of "Fast and Furious."

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:46.960
"Ask any racer, any real racer. It don't matter if&nbsp;
you win by an inch or a mile, winning's winning."

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.680
Finally, after months of this back and&nbsp;
forth jabbing, "The Fate of the Furious"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:57.680
premiered. Johnson and Diesel both appeared on&nbsp;
the April 8, 2017 red carpet in New York City,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.880
and they addressed their beef&nbsp;
in separate interviews with ET.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.680
Johnson said the disagreement had simply been due&nbsp;
to them having "different fundamental philosophies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.880
on how you do things." Diesel, in turn,&nbsp;
re-emphasized his previous "Uncle Dwayne" remark.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.080
In a different universe, that might have&nbsp;
been the end of it. But just like how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:18.560
"Fast and Furious" franchise refuses&nbsp;
to stop pumping out bombastic films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.040
the feud between Diesel and The Rock just&nbsp;
wouldn't go away. It wasn't long before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:27.280
battle heated up again, this time with&nbsp;
a third voice entering into the arena.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:35.440
"This idea of family that is so core to you that&nbsp;
it rules your world, it's a biological lie."

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.760
On October 4, 2017, "Fast and Furious"&nbsp;
costar Tyrese Gibson stepped into Diesel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.240
and Johnson's feud after the announcement&nbsp;
that the release date for "F9: The Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.800
Saga" had been significantly delayed. Many&nbsp;
presumed the delay was mostly due to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:57.040
impending spinoff film "Fast and Furious Presents:&nbsp;
Hobbs &amp; Shaw," starring Johnson and Jason Statham.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:02.160
Gibson appeared to believe the same thing, and he&nbsp;
didn't hold back in bashing The Rock on Instagram&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:06.400
for, quote, "making the fast and&nbsp;
the furious franchise about YOU."

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.240
Tyrese ended his post by saying that&nbsp;
he was, quote, "just a passionate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.760
film critic," and going hard at Johnson by&nbsp;
criticizing his turn in 2017's "Baywatch."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:21.440
After so many months of Diesel and The Rock subtly&nbsp;
going at each other one-on-one, Tyrese's post&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.960
stirred things up majorly in the public eye.&nbsp;
However, rather than pile on Johnson, Diesel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.600
jumped in with what appeared to be an attempt to&nbsp;
squash the beef before it heated up once again.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:37.200
Two days after Tyrese made his post, Diesel&nbsp;
took to Instagram with an even longer statement.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.920
"I know there has been a lot of speculation as to&nbsp;
why the Fast 9 release date was pushed. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:46.480
like any vehicle that has run around the globe 8&nbsp;
times, the franchise is in need of maintenance."

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.200
As a lead producer on the franchise, it makes&nbsp;
sense that Diesel would want "Hobbs &amp; Shaw"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:56.000
to find success, and his post seemed to show&nbsp;
full support for Johnson's spinoff endeavor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.640
For a while, things seemed&nbsp;
to be at peace once again.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:04.960
In a cover story interview with Rolling Stone&nbsp;
in April of 2018, Johnson was once again asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:10.000
about the feud with Diesel. Specifically, he was&nbsp;
asked whether or not the duo had actually shot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.800
any scenes together for "The Fate of the Furious,"&nbsp;
which was constructed in such a way that the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.480
never quite shared the screen. Johnson confirmed&nbsp;
this, but he left his reply simple and to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:25.200
point, reiterating his past sentiments about them&nbsp;
simply having different philosophies on things.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:30.320
Years later, in an October 2021 interview&nbsp;
with Vanity Fair, Johnson explained that not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:34.480
filming scenes with Diesel was one of his&nbsp;
conditions for returning to the franchise.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.720
"I wanted to forgo drama. I thought that that&nbsp;
was the best thing to do. For everybody."

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.920
That detail seems to confirm that&nbsp;
the tension between the two must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:45.920
have preceded production on "The Fate of the&nbsp;
Furious" by a significant amount of time.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.960
After the release of "Hobbs and Shaw," The&nbsp;
Rock took to his Instagram page to share an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:56.800
especially sweaty celebration video. Shot in what&nbsp;
appears to be his gym, Johnson thanked the cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:01.280
crew, and fans for making the spinoff film&nbsp;
a success and declared how proud he was to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.000
be a part of the "Fast and Furious" franchise.&nbsp;
Later in the video, he made a cryptic claim that

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:11.600
"Of course, all roads lead to one thing.&nbsp;
I'll be seeing you soon, Toretto."

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.000
Johnson didn't appear at all in "F9:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.560
The Fast Saga," which he claimed was due to&nbsp;
scheduling conflicts with "Hobbs &amp; Shaw."

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.000
For nearly two years, the beef lay dormant, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.600
it apparently never got squashed for good.&nbsp;
On June 22, 2021, Men's Health published a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:32.240
lengthy profile on Diesel where he once again&nbsp;
discussed his relationship with The Rock

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:36.480
"It was a tough character to embody, the&nbsp;
Hobbs character. My approach at the time was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.240
a lot of tough love to assist in getting&nbsp;
that performance where it needed to be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.720
I would do anything I'd have to do in order to&nbsp;
get performances in anything I'm producing."

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:48.080
Diesel seemed to be implying that his&nbsp;
rocky relationship with Johnson was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:51.440
partially meant to elicit a more&nbsp;
compelling performance on screen.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:57.760
The Rock had one simple thing to say about&nbsp;
Diesel's "tough love" comments in a July 21,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.320
2021 piece from The Hollywood Reporter.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.960
"I laughed and I laughed hard. I think everyone&nbsp;
had a laugh at that. And I'll leave it at that."

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:09.440
Sadly for fans, Johnson also revealed in&nbsp;
that same interview that he has no plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:14.320
of returning to the franchise for "Fast&nbsp;
and Furious 10" or "Fast and Furious 11."

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.440
"I wish them the best of luck&nbsp;
on Fast 10 and Fast 11 and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:21.200
rest of the Fast &amp; Furious movies&nbsp;
they do that will be without me."

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.600
After "F9: The Fast Saga" came and&nbsp;
went without even a mention of Hobbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.920
many fans assumed that they'd seen the&nbsp;
last of Johnson in the franchise. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.080
that might not actually be the end of Hobbs&nbsp;
— if Diesel has anything to say about it.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:41.280
On November 7, 2021, Diesel took to Instagram&nbsp;
once more to ask Johnson to return to "Fast and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:45.280
Furious." After all that had gone on between&nbsp;
them, the post came as a shock to many,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:49.680
but Diesel was clear about his desire to&nbsp;
bring Hobbs back into the fold. Diesel wrote,

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:54.480
"My little brother Dwayne... the time has&nbsp;
come. The world awaits the finale of Fast 10."

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.440
After some elegant words about the franchise's&nbsp;
legacy and a promise he made to Paul Walker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.760
Diesel ends with a clear call to action:

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.840
"Hobbs can't be played by no other.&nbsp;
I hope that you rise to the occasion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.360
and fulfill your destiny."

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.480
Obviously, a Hobbs return in "Fast and Furious&nbsp;
10" would be great for the overarching story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:16.800
of the franchise. The character has been a&nbsp;
part of the series' most successful films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.440
and he's a clear fan favorite. Plus, now&nbsp;
that John Cena has joined the series as Dom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:26.640
Toretto's estranged brother Jakob, there's&nbsp;
a chance for the two former WWE superstars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:31.680
to meet in one of history's biggest action&nbsp;
franchises. That's an exciting proposition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.120
but whether or not it will happen&nbsp;
is another question entirely.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:38.400
"You're stronger together. You always were."

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.680
As of the making of this video, Johnson&nbsp;
himself hasn't responded to Diesel's request&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.160
for him to return. However, his longtime&nbsp;
business partner Hiram Garcia has spoken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:52.720
publicly about the matter. In an interview&nbsp;
with Screen Rant published on November 14,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:57.760
2021, Garcia said he hadn't had much chance&nbsp;
to speak with The Rock about the idea.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:02.800
"Look, DJ's the biggest movie star in the world.&nbsp;
No one's below trying all attempts and approaches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:07.360
to try and get him on board. So I appreciate&nbsp;
it. You got to take your shot. You never know."

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:12.320
Though a bit condescending in tone, Garcia&nbsp;
isn't necessarily wrong in his assessment of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:17.920
situation. "Fast and Furious" was certainly a huge&nbsp;
launching platform for Johnson's international&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:23.040
stardom, but since then he's worked on building&nbsp;
his own franchises like "Jungle Cruise" or "Red&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:27.760
Notice." Getting him back on board with Diesel&nbsp;
and the rest of the "Fast and Furious" crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:32.240
could be a complicated process, and that's&nbsp;
assuming he even wants to come back at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:37.600
Still, there's hope that fans could see Dom&nbsp;
and Hobbs side by side once again sometime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:42.720
down the line. After all, "Fast and Furious" is&nbsp;
still a story about family, and as we all know…

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:47.840
"You don't turn your back on&nbsp;
family. Even when they do."

